the push to web api  let's have a look at the push web api  you will need to be logged in with your  aging face account which you can do by  executing this first cell or by typing  aging face minus cli login in a terminal  just enter your username and password  then click login  this will store an authentication token  in the cache of the machine you're using  now let's launch a fine tuning of a bird  model  on the glue collar data set  we won't go over the fine tuning code  because you can find it in any  transformers tutorial or by looking at  the videos linked below  what interests us here is how we can  leverage the model hub during training  this is done with the push to help equal  true argument passed in your training  arguments  this will automatically upload your  model to the app each time it is saved  so every epoch in our case  this allows you to resume training from  a different machine if the current one  gets interrupted  the model will be updated in your  namespace with the name of the output  directory you picked by default  you can choose another name by passing  it to the upmodel id argument  you can also push inside an organization  you are a member of by passing a full  repository name with the name of the  organization slash the model id you want  to pick  with that done we can just launch  training and wait a little bit  i'll cut the waiting time from the video  note that the model is pushed  asynchronously  meaning that the training continues  while your model is uploaded to the hub  when your first commit is finished you  can go inspect your model on the hub by  looking inside your namespace  and you will find it at the very top  you can even start playing with its  inference widget while it's continuing  the training  the collide dataset tasks the model with  determining if the sentence is  grammatically correct or not so we pick  an example of incorrect sentence to test  it  note that it will take a bit of time to  load your model inside the inference  apipe the first time you try to use it  we'll cut that time from the video  there is something wrong with the labels  but we'll fix it later in this video  once your training is finished  you should do one last push with the  trainer that pushed to a method  this is for two reasons  first this will make sure you're  uploading the final version of your  model if you didn't already for instance  if you used the save every n-step  strategy instead of every ebook  second this will draft a model card that  will be the landing page of your model  repo  once the commit is done let's go back on  our model page and refresh  we can see the draft of the model card  which includes information on which  pre-trained model we fine-tuned  the final evaluation lesson metric  the training hyper parameter used  the intermediate training results  and the framework versions we used so  that other people can easily reproduce  our results  on top of all that information the  trainer also included some metadata that  is interpreted by the urging face  website in the model card  you get the value of the matrix reported  in a nice widget as well as a link to a  leaderboard with paper with code  the tensorboard runs have also been  pushed to this repo and we can look at  them directly from the model hub by  clicking on the training metrics submenu  if you are not using the trainer api to  function your model you can use the push  tool method on the model and tokenizer  directly we'll use this to fix our  labels in the inference widget  the inference widget was using default  names for labels because we did not  indicate the correspondence between  integers and label names we can fix this  in the configuration by setting the  label to id and ad to label fields to  the proper values then pushing the modal  config to the hub  once this is done we can check on the  website and the modal is now showing the  proper label  now that the model is on the hub we can  use it from anywhere as we would any  other transformer model with the from  pre-trained method or with the pipeline  function  we just have to use the identifier from  the hub and we can see that the model  configuration and weights as well as the  tokenizer files are automatically  downloaded  try the push to web api on your next  training to easily share your model with  the rest of the world
 

